# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree, not just in the index.
#
# These run on the VPS under bash, and the pipeline's shell test harness runs
# them locally too. On Windows `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to CRLF on
# checkout, and bash then fails on the stray carriage return with errors like
# `$'\r': command not found`. The committed blobs are already LF, so this
# changes nothing about history — it only stops fresh clones and git worktrees
# from producing scripts that cannot run.
*.sh text eol=lf
